From: Prabha Murugesan <prabha.murugesan@morsemicro.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: disable automatic wlan interface creation on driver registration

Set IEEE80211_HW_NO_AUTO_VIF to prevent mac80211 from automatically
creating a default STA interface when the morse driver registers with
ieee80211_register_hw(). Interface creation is handled by the OpenWrt
wifi subsystem (mac80211.sh/netifd) via nl80211.

This ensures consistent behaviour across mac80211 versions (5.10 auto-
creates a default wlanX; 6.12 does not). With this flag, both versions
rely on userspace for interface management.

--- a/mac.c
+++ b/mac.c
@@ -6850,6 +6850,9 @@ static void morse_mac_config_ieee80211_hw(struct morse *mors, struct ieee80211_h
 {
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SIGNAL_DBM);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
+
+	/* Let userspace (OpenWrt netifd/mac80211.sh) manage interface creation */
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, NO_AUTO_VIF);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, REPORTS_TX_ACK_STATUS);

 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, AMPDU_AGGREGATION);
